<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56233" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καυνάκης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thick cloak</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				1137
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. πορφυροῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					972
				</span></i>
			; said to be of Persian or Babylonian make, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>An.</u>
				6.29.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.59
			</span></i>, cf. Sch.Ar.l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Semus
				20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				48.3
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PHib.</u>
				1.121.11
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καυνάκη</span></b> , ἡ, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				6.605
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαυνάκη</span> (which is also found in codd. of <i><span class="en">
				<u>Peripl.M.Rubr.</u>
				6
			</span></i>):—
				Dim.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καυνάκιον</span></b> , τό, <i><span class="en">
				Zonar.
			</span></i> (Assyr. <i>gaunakka</i> 'frilled and flounced
		mantle'.)</div>
